1
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:06,006
I shouldn't get distracted.

2
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:10,343
Michiko, just concentrate
and follow your instincts!

3
00:00:10,744 --> 00:00:11,578
In one, two.

4
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:17,250
It's useless, they're all cute!

5
00:00:19,652 --> 00:00:21,955
Especially this one!

6
00:00:24,624 --> 00:00:28,728
- How expensive!
- They're all so cute, I can't choose one.

7
00:00:28,795 --> 00:00:29,629
Okay.

8
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,431
All okay.

9
00:00:31,931 --> 00:00:33,533
I'll buy all the clothes on this hanger.

10
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,637
There comes another pair
of lovers shopping.

11
00:00:40,273 --> 00:00:41,141
Goodness!

12
00:00:41,674 --> 00:00:42,709
I'm very sorry!

13
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:44,411
Pick them up…now!

14
00:00:44,477 --> 00:00:45,712
Yes, sir.

15
00:00:46,312 --> 00:00:50,216
"Yes, sir"? I found another
who talks that way here.

16
00:00:50,283 --> 00:00:51,518
Have you decided?

17
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:55,422
Can I… put this on hold?

18
00:00:55,922 --> 00:00:57,891
Yes, for one week.

19
00:00:58,358 --> 00:01:00,960
- Then, yes, please.
- We will be waiting.

20
00:01:01,027 --> 00:01:01,861
Akira...

21
00:01:01,928 --> 00:01:05,198
Mr. Akira, is it a definite "no"?

22
00:01:05,265 --> 00:01:07,634
Yes, a definite no.

23
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,737
The brand new cloth…is so cute!

24
00:01:10,804 --> 00:01:14,240
I'll do perform many operations,
so please lend me the money.

25
00:01:14,307 --> 00:01:17,177
Michiko, you're at your last straw.

26
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:19,879
Toutei hospital could decide
to fire you at any time.

27
00:01:19,946 --> 00:01:23,083
If that old lady Kubo's coup succeeds,

28
00:01:23,149 --> 00:01:25,852
it will be a straight goodbye for you.

29
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:28,254
What do you mean? You mean I'll be fired?

30
00:01:28,321 --> 00:01:30,423
Yes. I don't have money

31
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:33,326
to loan to an unemployed person.

32
00:01:34,027 --> 00:01:38,965
Okay. Wait, no! Please.
I want that brand new cloth.

33
00:01:40,533 --> 00:01:43,803
Ben Casey. Loan me some money!

34
00:01:44,704 --> 00:01:48,141
See? Even Ben Casey is saying no!

35
00:01:48,208 --> 00:01:49,342
How stingy!

36
00:01:49,409 --> 00:01:52,679
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

37
00:01:52,745 --> 00:01:53,580
It hurts.

38
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:58,518
<i>In 2016, the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

39
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:01,254
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>

40
00:02:01,321 --> 00:02:03,156
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

41
00:02:03,523 --> 00:02:05,058
Did you get an answer?

42
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:07,360
It has turned out...

43
00:02:07,427 --> 00:02:10,063
that this thesis completely plagiarised...

44
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:13,233
from Professor John Starkey's paper.

45
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:15,101
Write your letter of resignation now.

46
00:02:17,704 --> 00:02:20,707
I have thought very carefully...

47
00:02:22,175 --> 00:02:28,948
about what is the most important...
for Toutei University Hospital.

48
00:02:29,015 --> 00:02:31,017
You finally decided to quit?

49
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:34,087
That is a wise judgment.

50
00:02:34,888 --> 00:02:36,623
<i>Famous hospitals use...</i>

51
00:02:37,123 --> 00:02:39,425
<i>their brand power to push</i>
<i>into the global world.</i>

52
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:42,695
<i>On the other hand, highly skilled surgeons</i>

53
00:02:42,762 --> 00:02:45,999
<i>in pursuit of a higher salary</i>
<i>were relocating to foreign countries.</i>

54
00:02:46,065 --> 00:02:48,134
Wait, the world famous Kitano isn't here.

55
00:02:48,201 --> 00:02:50,470
I heard he went to an academic
meeting in New York.

56
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:53,806
He won't have to get involved
in the power struggle in hospital.

57
00:02:53,873 --> 00:02:56,176
The superstar is quite good
at managing crises.

58
00:02:56,242 --> 00:02:59,646
He's just sly. He's always been like that.

59
00:02:59,712 --> 00:03:01,181
You're pathetic as always.

60
00:03:03,316 --> 00:03:06,386
<i>The world of medicine has entered</i>

61
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:10,023
into the global world
of survival of the fittest.

62
00:03:11,925 --> 00:03:12,926
<i>In the midst of it,</i>

63
00:03:13,259 --> 00:03:16,529
<i>a new breed of doctor has emerged.</i>
<i>Freelance doctors,</i>

64
00:03:16,596 --> 00:03:19,632
<i>in other words, lone doctors.</i>

65
00:03:19,699 --> 00:03:23,836
I desperately want it. I want it so bad.

66
00:03:24,671 --> 00:03:27,974
Let me operate! Let me operate!

67
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:35,615
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

68
00:03:36,249 --> 00:03:40,587
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority,</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

69
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:44,290
<i>Her solo weapons are</i>
<i>her license and the skills</i>

70
00:03:44,824 --> 00:03:46,292
<i>she has earned.</i>

71
00:03:46,359 --> 00:03:49,162
Hey. Is something going on?

72
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:52,031
It may be a historic day.

73
00:03:52,498 --> 00:03:53,733
Mountains may be moved.

74
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,535
What mountain? Mount Fuji?

75
00:03:55,602 --> 00:03:59,205
Idiot. Director Hiruma will announce
resignation before the media.

76
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:02,342
Seriously?

77
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:10,550
Yes, seriously. You're so loud.
You scared me.

78
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,388
She stole it from me.

79
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:18,157
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

80
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:21,928
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

81
00:04:37,543 --> 00:04:41,047
Let's begin the urgent conference now.

82
00:04:42,849 --> 00:04:44,217
It doesn't even suit her.

83
00:04:45,918 --> 00:04:50,023
Thank you for your attendance
despite your busy schedules.

84
00:04:50,590 --> 00:04:52,592
Concerning the thesis
plagiarism incident...

85
00:04:52,659 --> 00:04:54,827
that occurred several days ago,

86
00:04:55,395 --> 00:04:59,666
Director Hiruma would like...
to personally make an announcement.

87
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:09,208
I am Shigekatsu Hiruma...
from Toutei University Hospital...

88
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:15,248
and I have called this meeting today.

89
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:16,816
Why is he so calm?

90
00:05:16,883 --> 00:05:18,618
He'll announce resignation, right?

91
00:05:18,685 --> 00:05:21,988
First of all, the claims...

92
00:05:22,722 --> 00:05:24,724
regarding the plagiarism of

93
00:05:25,291 --> 00:05:31,364
Professor John Starkey's thesis...
is not true.

94
00:05:32,065 --> 00:05:33,533
What are you talking about?

95
00:05:34,767 --> 00:05:36,169
Let me introduce you.

96
00:05:38,204 --> 00:05:41,574
Here's the professor
of Harvard Medical School,

97
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:47,847
Professor... John…Starkey!

98
00:06:00,059 --> 00:06:01,594
It's the all okay guy.

99
00:06:10,737 --> 00:06:11,838
What?

100
00:06:11,904 --> 00:06:13,373
Dr. Ebina is here too.

101
00:06:13,439 --> 00:06:15,041
Try to stay calm.

102
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:17,276
- It happened.
- You dumb.

103
00:06:30,256 --> 00:06:31,324
Well,

104
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:32,992
I'm Dr. Ebina.

105
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:35,728
I graduated from Toutei University
and currently serve...

106
00:06:36,095 --> 00:06:38,097
the national Kodo Medical Centre
as the chief of surgery department.

107
00:06:38,164 --> 00:06:39,999
- Ebina?
- Why is Ebina here?

108
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:41,300
Did he go back to Kanazawa?

109
00:06:41,367 --> 00:06:43,136
I heard he went once around.

110
00:06:43,202 --> 00:06:46,439
Let me make it clear
about the suspected thesis.

111
00:06:46,506 --> 00:06:49,876
I and Professor Rock Shrimp

112
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:54,747
from Harvard Medical...
wrote the thesis together...

113
00:06:55,615 --> 00:06:58,284
based on Professor Starkey's work.

114
00:06:58,351 --> 00:06:59,419
He's lying.

115
00:06:59,485 --> 00:07:00,753
Who'd believe that?

116
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:03,022
The definition of plagiarism

117
00:07:03,089 --> 00:07:06,058
is using…someone else's work
and publishing it as your own.

118
00:07:06,125 --> 00:07:07,126
Right, Mr. Hara?

119
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:08,494
Pardon?

120
00:07:08,561 --> 00:07:13,833
However, this thesis…was created
with Toutei Hospital staff,

121
00:07:14,534 --> 00:07:16,702
so no plagiarism was involved.

122
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:22,508
Despite this fact, some kept insisting
that it was plagiarism and fraud.

123
00:07:22,575 --> 00:07:27,280
They brought dishonour
on Toutei University Hospital,

124
00:07:27,346 --> 00:07:29,182
in order to tarnish the image
of the hospital.

125
00:07:29,615 --> 00:07:32,218
Right? Ms. Kubo.

126
00:07:33,352 --> 00:07:35,154
Dr. Saionji.

127
00:07:36,522 --> 00:07:38,624
Dr. Kikawada.

128
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:44,297
Our Toutei University Hospital...
would like to use this opportunity...

129
00:07:45,331 --> 00:07:47,433
to announce a new thesis

130
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:52,338
that's co-authored...
by Dr. Starkey and Dr. Ebina.

131
00:07:57,810 --> 00:07:59,378
Resection of
big hepatocellular carcinoma...

132
00:07:59,912 --> 00:08:02,949
in atria without open heart surgery.

133
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:06,953
We have developed a method
that has never been done before.

134
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:11,624
The surgery that opens...
hearts using a heart-lung machine...

135
00:08:11,691 --> 00:08:14,494
takes a large toll on patients.

136
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,395
- Right, Dr. Kaji.
- He tries to drag me into it.

137
00:08:16,462 --> 00:08:20,233
However, this surgery method...
doesn't impose such burdens,

138
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,969
and the risk of postoperative
complication is way far lower.

139
00:08:23,803 --> 00:08:25,037
It is a perfect technique.

140
00:08:25,104 --> 00:08:26,339
We call it...

141
00:08:26,806 --> 00:08:31,477
Toutei University Hospital's
2016 Fall Special Surgery Method.

142
00:08:33,112 --> 00:08:36,315
Without challenges,
there can be no success.

143
00:08:41,954 --> 00:08:44,590
There he goes again.

144
00:08:55,001 --> 00:08:56,802
Where is the customary gift?

145
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:57,904
Here you are.

146
00:09:00,406 --> 00:09:05,344
I'm not sure if you like the
Japanese taste, but please try it.

147
00:09:15,488 --> 00:09:17,490
Dr. Ebina,

148
00:09:18,157 --> 00:09:19,191
I never thought

149
00:09:19,258 --> 00:09:22,161
you'd attend the same meeting...
with Dr. Starkey.

150
00:09:25,097 --> 00:09:27,233
I guess someone is watching over me.

151
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:30,770
- I'm honoured to be of help.
- You did great, Ebina.

152
00:09:30,836 --> 00:09:31,904
Yes sir.

153
00:09:32,438 --> 00:09:35,608
So in other words,
Ebina saved the director.

154
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:39,478
So that director didn't fall
into the trap after all.

155
00:09:39,545 --> 00:09:42,982
I guess Kubo's dream
to rule the hospital is over.

156
00:09:43,049 --> 00:09:47,086
Well, we don't know that yet.
That old lady is so persistent.

157
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:51,457
It's pretty pathetic that Director
Hiruma has only one friend, Ebina.

158
00:09:51,857 --> 00:09:53,693
What's wrong Michiko? It's your turn.

159
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:54,860
Okay.

160
00:09:55,494 --> 00:09:56,596
Hey Akira,

161
00:09:56,662 --> 00:10:00,499
have you ever…removed hepatocellular
carcinoma from atrium?

162
00:10:00,566 --> 00:10:04,203
I haven't. It's quite a difficult surgery.

163
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:07,073
Is that the new thesis
by Ebina and Starkey is about?

164
00:10:07,139 --> 00:10:11,177
That's right. They plan to challenge it
without open heart surgery.

165
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:15,615
A liver tumour has grown
into the heart, right?

166
00:10:15,681 --> 00:10:18,250
Can they do that surgery
without a scalpel?

167
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:21,988
They will neither use a heart-lung machine
nor scalpels.

168
00:10:22,054 --> 00:10:24,590
- How are they going to do that?
- It's impossible.

169
00:10:24,657 --> 00:10:25,524
Impossible.

170
00:10:25,591 --> 00:10:28,594
It's rumoured that Starkey
is the American version...

171
00:10:28,661 --> 00:10:31,397
of the money loving, power hungry Hiruma.

172
00:10:32,031 --> 00:10:35,368
- I doubt he's good at operating.
- Really?

173
00:10:37,370 --> 00:10:39,872
- Michiko? I win!
- Yes?

174
00:10:39,939 --> 00:10:41,774
- There you are.
- Gosh.

175
00:10:41,841 --> 00:10:45,011
And another! A million stones!

176
00:10:45,945 --> 00:10:48,114
What do you mean a million stones?

177
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:53,185
Did you really not know…that
Professor Starkey was coming to Japan?

178
00:10:53,753 --> 00:10:54,920
We've very sorry.

179
00:10:56,155 --> 00:10:57,023
You dimwits.

180
00:10:58,290 --> 00:10:59,191
Meat!

181
00:10:59,258 --> 00:11:00,926
Oh, yes ma'am.

182
00:11:05,097 --> 00:11:07,266
- It's good when it's rare.
- Let me serve...

183
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,169
Put them both in.

184
00:11:10,236 --> 00:11:11,404
Yes ma'am.

185
00:11:14,473 --> 00:11:18,644
Don't you two have any idea
how to turn this situation around?

186
00:11:19,712 --> 00:11:23,015
- Aren't you chiefs?
- Deputy Director, if I may...

187
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:26,485
There is no necessity to turn this around.

188
00:11:27,386 --> 00:11:28,220
What do you mean?

189
00:11:28,287 --> 00:11:32,291
Ebina and Starkey's... new thesis,

190
00:11:32,925 --> 00:11:36,295
is confirmed to be an empty theory
with no clinical proof.

191
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:37,663
An empty theory?

192
00:11:37,730 --> 00:11:39,799
Even if they were...
to attempt the surgery,

193
00:11:40,466 --> 00:11:43,202
there is no chance of success.

194
00:11:45,471 --> 00:11:46,539
If that's the case,

195
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:51,277
then why is Hiruma...
trying to perform the surgery?

196
00:11:51,343 --> 00:11:52,645
That is...

197
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:53,713
That is what?

198
00:11:57,616 --> 00:11:59,251
Well...

199
00:11:59,685 --> 00:12:02,755
You don't know? You're useless.

200
00:12:02,822 --> 00:12:04,356
- I'm sorry.
- Eat some vegetables.

201
00:12:05,157 --> 00:12:06,225
- Yes ma'am.
- Yes ma'am.

202
00:12:07,193 --> 00:12:08,027
- Use this.
- Okay.

203
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:13,666
Director Hiruma,
It's about the new thesis.

204
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,668
The operation is impossible, right?

205
00:12:16,836 --> 00:12:17,670
You knew that?

206
00:12:17,737 --> 00:12:23,142
Ebina, I don't care if the
operation is doable or not.

207
00:12:24,343 --> 00:12:25,778
What's important here...

208
00:12:27,813 --> 00:12:29,782
is to show the firm determination...

209
00:12:30,216 --> 00:12:34,653
of our Toutei University Hospital
to the world...

210
00:12:35,054 --> 00:12:38,491
to challenge the operation...
which is regarded to be impossible.

211
00:12:38,557 --> 00:12:41,026
What if they find out we can't...

212
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:45,564
What? "Resection of giant
hepatocellular carcinoma..."

213
00:12:45,631 --> 00:12:50,202
"with intra-atrial extension
without open-heart surgery."

214
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:52,371
In the first place,

215
00:12:53,873 --> 00:12:59,578
where do you plan to find a patient...
who would need this surgery?

216
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:05,017
I looked through all of the databases,

217
00:13:06,819 --> 00:13:11,323
however I couldn't find
a single patient…who fit the role.

218
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:15,995
It's impossible to operate
if the patient doesn't exist.

219
00:13:16,061 --> 00:13:20,633
You really are a genius, Director Hiruma!

220
00:13:21,767 --> 00:13:24,804
Saionji and Kikawada are here.

221
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:25,838
With what business?

222
00:13:35,281 --> 00:13:39,451
Saionji merely stated, that he
would like to make an inquiry.

223
00:13:45,257 --> 00:13:49,361
Kikawada would like to apologise
for his rude behaviours.

224
00:13:50,229 --> 00:13:54,567
Then, Ms. Shiromizu,
please tell them this.

225
00:14:07,947 --> 00:14:09,315
"I have no business with you.

226
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:11,517
Get out of my sight immediately", he said.

227
00:14:11,584 --> 00:14:13,018
- Please wait.
- Sir...

228
00:14:13,085 --> 00:14:15,988
- We are so sorry!
- We are so sorry!

229
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:18,424
What foolish people.

230
00:14:19,058 --> 00:14:21,360
What should I do with them, Ebina?

231
00:14:21,794 --> 00:14:23,596
Show your loyalty to Director Hiruma.

232
00:14:25,064 --> 00:14:27,032
Director Hiruma, Long live your majesty!

233
00:14:27,099 --> 00:14:28,200
Louder! Long live your majesty!

234
00:14:28,267 --> 00:14:31,370
- Long live your majesty!
- Long live your majesty!

235
00:14:33,973 --> 00:14:35,074
You're too loud.

236
00:14:36,642 --> 00:14:39,078
Are you going home already?

237
00:14:39,144 --> 00:14:40,479
Yes, take care.

238
00:14:53,626 --> 00:14:55,294
Well...

239
00:15:02,468 --> 00:15:04,770
What do you mean God chose you?

240
00:15:04,837 --> 00:15:07,373
- Please take care. Thank you.
- Hey.

241
00:15:07,439 --> 00:15:08,807
Thank you.

242
00:15:12,478 --> 00:15:15,080
Shrimp! Dr. Shrimp!

243
00:15:15,147 --> 00:15:16,315
Get off of him.

244
00:15:20,853 --> 00:15:23,455
We need to examine him immediately.

245
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:26,759
Hey, someone! Someone fell!

246
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:30,529
He has to go through an examination! Hey!

247
00:15:39,571 --> 00:15:41,307
He has a large tumour on his liver...

248
00:15:41,907 --> 00:15:43,509
that has progressed

249
00:15:43,909 --> 00:15:47,079
from the inferior vena cava...
to the right atrium.

250
00:15:47,146 --> 00:15:50,516
That's right. It's a hepatocellular
carcinoma in the atrium.

251
00:15:52,151 --> 00:15:55,888
This patient is perfect for your thesis.

252
00:15:59,525 --> 00:16:00,359
Twist of fate?

253
00:16:03,529 --> 00:16:04,897
A scandalous affair?

254
00:16:07,933 --> 00:16:10,569
It has nothing to do with a fate
or scandal.

255
00:16:17,176 --> 00:16:20,112
Professor Starkey, please wait.

256
00:16:20,746 --> 00:16:22,481
So you want us to cure his illness...

257
00:16:22,548 --> 00:16:24,216
here at Toutei?

258
00:16:25,884 --> 00:16:27,586
He's forcing a patient to stay here.

259
00:16:40,299 --> 00:16:44,903
I apologise, I put a large
burden on you, Dr. Ebina.

260
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:47,106
Please don't worry about me.

261
00:16:47,539 --> 00:16:49,208
Let's think about

262
00:16:49,274 --> 00:16:51,343
what treatment would be best for you.

263
00:16:52,778 --> 00:16:56,181
However, we do not need to operate.

264
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:57,583
We're not going to operate?

265
00:16:58,150 --> 00:16:59,084
No one can perform the surgery.

266
00:16:59,151 --> 00:17:02,621
Really? Then why did you
write that thesis?

267
00:17:10,996 --> 00:17:12,765
You're the one who wrote it, right?

268
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:16,035
You wrote it, knowing
you had this illness,

269
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:20,506
so you hoped that it could save your life.

270
00:17:25,577 --> 00:17:26,779
Let me operate on you.

271
00:17:28,113 --> 00:17:29,448
You?

272
00:17:29,515 --> 00:17:30,749
I never fail.

273
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:40,859
You do not have permission to operate.

274
00:17:41,293 --> 00:17:43,262
- What?
- It's Director Hiruma's order.

275
00:17:43,695 --> 00:17:46,165
He came to the conclusion
that there is no patient...

276
00:17:47,199 --> 00:17:48,767
who would need the surgery of the thesis.

277
00:17:48,834 --> 00:17:51,703
What is he talking about? It is right
in front of us! Isn't he an idiot?

278
00:17:51,770 --> 00:17:53,238
- Take her out of here.
- Yes sir.

279
00:17:54,039 --> 00:17:55,240
What?

280
00:17:55,307 --> 00:17:57,009
Let go!

281
00:17:58,177 --> 00:18:00,312
If he doesn't get the surgery, he'll die.

282
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:02,681
How dare you call yourselves doctors.

283
00:18:03,315 --> 00:18:08,187
Please go back to
the U.S. immediately, Dr. Shrimp.

284
00:18:10,289 --> 00:18:12,624
Dr. Ebina, you must return to Kanazawa.

285
00:18:13,225 --> 00:18:15,260
There is no place for you here.

286
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:24,970
Dr. Ebina,

287
00:18:25,904 --> 00:18:29,641
my illness...
cannot be cured without surgery.

288
00:18:30,075 --> 00:18:31,977
Moreover, as my kidneys are failing,

289
00:18:32,044 --> 00:18:34,646
using a heart-lung machine is too risky.

290
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:38,317
That is why I needed...

291
00:18:38,383 --> 00:18:40,819
a procedure
that doesn't involve a scalpel.

292
00:18:42,888 --> 00:18:44,456
That's why you wrote that thesis?

293
00:18:44,523 --> 00:18:48,160
I thought maybe someone who read it
would accept the challenge.

294
00:18:50,162 --> 00:18:52,865
It was just a glimpse of hope I had.

295
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:55,667
Dr. Shrimp.

296
00:18:56,869 --> 00:18:57,836
I'm leaving.

297
00:18:57,903 --> 00:18:59,304
You can't.

298
00:19:00,672 --> 00:19:04,109
I cannot let you leave like this,
as a fellow doctor,

299
00:19:04,176 --> 00:19:07,846
Dr. Ebina,
you cannot perform this surgery.

300
00:19:10,015 --> 00:19:13,819
No matter what, I cannot
stand against Dr. Starkey.

301
00:19:15,721 --> 00:19:18,190
For someone like me to become a Professor,

302
00:19:19,057 --> 00:19:21,360
I had to fully commit myself to Starkey.

303
00:19:23,629 --> 00:19:25,831
If he told me to wipe his bottom,
I wiped it.

304
00:19:27,566 --> 00:19:29,635
If he said to lick his shoes,
I licked them.

305
00:19:30,035 --> 00:19:33,405
After flattering him again and again,

306
00:19:34,606 --> 00:19:36,608
I finally got to where I am now.

307
00:19:39,077 --> 00:19:40,212
You are the same.

308
00:19:41,613 --> 00:19:44,016
You cannot go against
what Director Hiruma says.

309
00:19:46,051 --> 00:19:47,452
I understand that.

310
00:19:53,792 --> 00:19:55,327
So Dr. Shrimp could write

311
00:19:55,394 --> 00:19:58,363
such a difficult thesis...
because it was his case.

312
00:19:58,430 --> 00:20:01,633
But Director Hiruma not allowing
him to get surgery is horrible.

313
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:05,170
I know. All that hospital cares
is the brand value of the hospital.

314
00:20:05,237 --> 00:20:06,438
It's so bizarre.

315
00:20:06,505 --> 00:20:07,940
You're right.

316
00:20:08,407 --> 00:20:10,175
- She's here.
- The weeping old man.

317
00:20:10,242 --> 00:20:11,176
I'm not an old man.

318
00:20:11,243 --> 00:20:13,278
This is unexpected, Ms. Kubo.

319
00:20:13,345 --> 00:20:16,515
- What brings you here?
- I came to talk to Dr. Daimon.

320
00:20:16,582 --> 00:20:17,849
Me?

321
00:20:25,257 --> 00:20:27,125
But before that...

322
00:20:29,561 --> 00:20:33,131
I never thought you'd like mah-jong.

323
00:20:33,198 --> 00:20:34,266
You may not believe it,

324
00:20:34,333 --> 00:20:37,202
but I learned it before.

325
00:20:37,269 --> 00:20:39,238
They called
me a "Crying girl from the east."

326
00:20:39,304 --> 00:20:41,740
- A crying girl from the east?
- Here you go.

327
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:47,646
- Plop! East!
- Goodness.

328
00:20:47,713 --> 00:20:49,414
How scary.

329
00:20:50,015 --> 00:20:53,619
This is a big one. Here it goes.

330
00:20:54,853 --> 00:20:56,054
Yes! I win!

331
00:20:56,121 --> 00:20:59,358
I have collected all of them!

332
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:01,460
Michiko. What do you think you're doing?

333
00:21:01,526 --> 00:21:04,263
Don't worry about it.

334
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:05,964
Plop.

335
00:21:06,565 --> 00:21:07,566
Thank you.

336
00:21:08,066 --> 00:21:10,435
Do you want to go for another round?

337
00:21:11,536 --> 00:21:15,774
If I win, help me bring down Hiruma.

338
00:21:16,642 --> 00:21:18,710
Is that what you wanted to talk about?

339
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:23,382
Didn't you…operate on a patient
without permission and succeed?

340
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:25,717
Director Hiruma is just
becoming arrogant...

341
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:28,220
and it aggravates the corruption
within the hospital.

342
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:31,790
I just want to clean up the hospital.

343
00:21:31,857 --> 00:21:35,460
In order to do that, I must
bring down Hiruma…or I won't win.

344
00:21:37,696 --> 00:21:41,400
Your win or loss
has nothing to do with me.

345
00:21:42,501 --> 00:21:46,138
I know you just want
to gain the influence over everyone.

346
00:21:46,605 --> 00:21:50,442
Don't use a patient's life
as a pawn in your power struggle.

347
00:21:53,679 --> 00:21:55,881
I'm done!

348
00:21:55,947 --> 00:22:00,385
- Michiko!
- I'm done! I'm done!

349
00:22:00,452 --> 00:22:02,321
She's not learning anything.

350
00:22:02,387 --> 00:22:06,258
I apologise.
I will instruct her very carefully.

351
00:22:13,565 --> 00:22:15,667
If he told me to wipe his bottom,
I wiped it.

352
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:18,570
If he told me to lick his shoes,
I licked them.

353
00:22:18,637 --> 00:22:22,140
After flattering him again and again,

354
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:24,976
I finally got to where I am now.

355
00:22:28,313 --> 00:22:29,548
You are the same.

356
00:22:30,382 --> 00:22:32,718
You cannot go against
what Director Hiruma says.

357
00:22:36,288 --> 00:22:37,322
We are not the same.

358
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:40,325
I never licked his shoes.

359
00:22:42,828 --> 00:22:43,795
I am different.

360
00:22:45,497 --> 00:22:46,331
I am different.

361
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:50,168
You idiot!

362
00:22:50,235 --> 00:22:52,237
AOOKAYAMA TABLE TENNIS

363
00:22:55,574 --> 00:22:57,476
That old lady's really
getting on my nerves!

364
00:22:57,542 --> 00:23:00,178
Still you can't run amok.

365
00:23:00,245 --> 00:23:01,580
Why not?

366
00:23:01,646 --> 00:23:04,816
Both the director and Deputy Director
are telling you not to.

367
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:07,753
If you defy both of them,
you will be fired immediately.

368
00:23:07,819 --> 00:23:11,990
That's what irritates me so much!
I'm so good!

369
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:17,162
Michiko, there's another again.

370
00:23:21,566 --> 00:23:24,002
Daimon, let's have a match.

371
00:23:25,604 --> 00:23:27,072
Even you are here for a match?

372
00:23:27,139 --> 00:23:28,607
Just one round.

373
00:23:30,675 --> 00:23:34,913
If I win, I will...
let you operate on Dr. Shrimp.

374
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:35,981
What?

375
00:23:36,515 --> 00:23:39,418
What do you think? It's a promise.

376
00:23:48,059 --> 00:23:49,027
Ai?

377
00:24:06,411 --> 00:24:08,246
Yes!

378
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:13,251
That was a nice serve, but you lost.

379
00:24:17,689 --> 00:24:20,225
No matter if you won or lost,
I planned to operate.

380
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:22,027
I don't care what you say.

381
00:24:22,093 --> 00:24:23,028
Michiko.

382
00:24:24,162 --> 00:24:24,996
I have made a decision.

383
00:24:25,664 --> 00:24:28,733
I will lead the operation.
And you'll assist me.

384
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:32,737
What? I thought you said
no one can perform this operation.

385
00:24:32,804 --> 00:24:35,707
Yes, that is why I need you
as my assistant.

386
00:24:36,241 --> 00:24:39,010
Dr. Ebina, are you really okay with this?

387
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:45,116
Pushing ahead with the operation means...
standing against Director Hiruma.

388
00:24:46,718 --> 00:24:50,555
I am a doctor. I want to save lives.

389
00:24:50,622 --> 00:24:55,460
You might have to pay dear.
It may mess up your life.

390
00:24:56,394 --> 00:24:57,229
I'm aware of it.

391
00:24:59,865 --> 00:25:00,799
Thank you in advance.

392
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:22,087
The time has come for Dr. Ebina.

393
00:25:23,455 --> 00:25:24,589
Is that so?

394
00:25:30,896 --> 00:25:35,667
I will be performing...
Dr. Shrimp's operation tomorrow.

395
00:25:36,401 --> 00:25:41,439
You are going to ignore my order...
and operate?

396
00:25:43,542 --> 00:25:46,945
You sure have become something else.

397
00:25:47,012 --> 00:25:52,284
I will…make sure
the operation is a success.

398
00:25:53,685 --> 00:25:57,389
With no mistake, it will become
the world's first medical case,

399
00:25:58,523 --> 00:26:00,125
What will you do if you fail the surgery?

400
00:26:02,694 --> 00:26:04,029
I'll never be a scapegoat.

401
00:26:04,729 --> 00:26:08,099
I'll drag you into all this...

402
00:26:09,734 --> 00:26:10,802
and reveal everything to the public.

403
00:26:12,003 --> 00:26:13,071
What?

404
00:26:13,538 --> 00:26:15,073
In the event of success,

405
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:21,846
I need you to have a position…prepared
for me at Toutei University Hospital.

406
00:26:23,548 --> 00:26:24,382
A position?

407
00:26:24,449 --> 00:26:25,383
And then,

408
00:26:26,818 --> 00:26:28,353
do not ever oppose me...

409
00:26:30,855 --> 00:26:32,390
from now on.

410
00:26:36,127 --> 00:26:38,330
Are you seriously saying this?

411
00:26:40,899 --> 00:26:42,100
Here is a pen.

412
00:26:50,408 --> 00:26:51,543
Here is a written oath.

413
00:26:54,479 --> 00:26:55,614
Sign here.

414
00:26:56,314 --> 00:26:57,716
OATH

415
00:27:09,427 --> 00:27:13,198
Satoru Ebina. How dare you...

416
00:27:13,665 --> 00:27:14,799
It's Takashi Ebina.

417
00:27:16,601 --> 00:27:17,435
I need you to make a decision.

418
00:27:38,223 --> 00:27:42,327
Michiko, how do you plan to
do the operation tomorrow?

419
00:27:42,394 --> 00:27:44,396
You must have a plan, right?

420
00:27:45,363 --> 00:27:48,333
I'm not sure until I try.

421
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:52,203
The vital techniques were not
stated in the thesis, were they?

422
00:27:52,270 --> 00:27:55,840
You're right.

423
00:27:57,575 --> 00:27:58,910
It's no good.

424
00:28:02,714 --> 00:28:05,417
Here we go.

425
00:28:08,386 --> 00:28:11,556
What is that? I thought you were
thinking about the operation.

426
00:28:11,623 --> 00:28:12,457
Are you just trying
to solve the puzzle ring?

427
00:28:13,758 --> 00:28:15,760
This one is difficult.

428
00:28:17,896 --> 00:28:22,434
Bring one to the other, put them together,

429
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:24,703
and turn it around.

430
00:28:25,637 --> 00:28:27,839
Michiko, dinner is ready.

431
00:28:29,507 --> 00:28:33,645
Put them together,

432
00:28:34,479 --> 00:28:38,483
turn it over...

433
00:28:46,791 --> 00:28:49,060
So we did get entangled in this after all.

434
00:28:49,127 --> 00:28:50,895
You're brave.

435
00:28:51,796 --> 00:28:52,997
We both are.

436
00:28:53,798 --> 00:28:56,901
My fellows,
I'll make sure it does good for you.

437
00:28:58,069 --> 00:28:59,137
It begins soon.

438
00:29:03,975 --> 00:29:04,876
Daimon.

439
00:29:10,048 --> 00:29:11,683
OPERATING

440
00:29:12,817 --> 00:29:15,620
We will now begin the removal

441
00:29:15,687 --> 00:29:18,857
of the tumour within the atrium...
without open heart surgery.

442
00:29:18,923 --> 00:29:20,158
Let's do our best.

443
00:29:20,225 --> 00:29:21,359
Let's do our best.

444
00:29:21,426 --> 00:29:24,229
Vitals are 120 and 73.

445
00:29:24,295 --> 00:29:25,930
Heart rate is 82. Sinus rhythm is normal.

446
00:29:27,398 --> 00:29:28,266
Daimon.

447
00:29:30,268 --> 00:29:31,336
That was fast.

448
00:29:31,402 --> 00:29:32,704
From the beginning?

449
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:34,706
Didn't you say you are going to
make the abdominal incision.

450
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:42,847
There is a battle I cannot lose.

451
00:29:42,914 --> 00:29:45,116
Where?

452
00:29:45,183 --> 00:29:46,251
- Scalpel.
- Here.

453
00:29:48,186 --> 00:29:49,888
How did this happen?

454
00:29:51,022 --> 00:29:52,791
It seems like Director Hiruma approved.

455
00:29:53,625 --> 00:29:57,462
Even so, using Daimon as an ally...

456
00:29:57,529 --> 00:30:00,932
is a tactical move by Ebina.

457
00:30:06,104 --> 00:30:08,273
OPERATING HOUR

458
00:30:09,507 --> 00:30:12,477
You're always great at surgery.

459
00:30:19,150 --> 00:30:20,852
I have finished dissecting the liver.

460
00:30:29,327 --> 00:30:30,395
Daimon, what's wrong?

461
00:30:31,162 --> 00:30:33,097
I cannot follow the thesis
from this point on.

462
00:30:33,164 --> 00:30:35,200
What do you mean?

463
00:30:35,266 --> 00:30:36,701
If I do, I will fail.

464
00:30:37,769 --> 00:30:39,838
Michiko Daimon will fail?

465
00:30:40,605 --> 00:30:43,741
It happened because he tried
something he's incapable of.

466
00:30:45,610 --> 00:30:49,681
Please, you can do it Daimon.
I know you can.

467
00:30:50,481 --> 00:30:53,284
After putting them together...

468
00:30:54,419 --> 00:30:55,486
We don't have time.

469
00:30:58,756 --> 00:30:59,724
Hey.

470
00:31:01,092 --> 00:31:02,327
Hey,

471
00:31:02,393 --> 00:31:03,361
what's wrong?

472
00:31:04,762 --> 00:31:07,966
Daimon! Resume the operation!

473
00:31:08,833 --> 00:31:09,801
Daimon!

474
00:31:11,769 --> 00:31:13,771
You never fail!

475
00:31:16,140 --> 00:31:17,842
We don't have time.

476
00:31:19,177 --> 00:31:21,646
We are changing to an open heart surgery.

477
00:31:22,113 --> 00:31:23,381
Prepare the heart-lung machine.

478
00:31:23,448 --> 00:31:24,515
Sorry?

479
00:31:26,851 --> 00:31:28,319
- Prepare for open heart surgery.
- Got it.

480
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:29,420
Hurry up.

481
00:31:29,487 --> 00:31:31,055
- Bring stanozolol.
- Yes, sir.

482
00:31:31,122 --> 00:31:32,190
Then, what about...

483
00:31:32,257 --> 00:31:34,525
the Toutei University Hospital
2016 Fall Special Operation?

484
00:31:37,161 --> 00:31:40,832
Forget it. I can't just let him die
this way.

485
00:31:41,833 --> 00:31:44,969
Goodness, what is he talking about?

486
00:31:45,036 --> 00:31:46,437
Will they fail in either way?

487
00:31:46,871 --> 00:31:49,407
Let's open him up.

488
00:31:49,474 --> 00:31:50,308
- Scalpel.
- Yes, sir.

489
00:31:50,375 --> 00:31:52,110
Using a heart-lung machine on a patient...

490
00:31:52,610 --> 00:31:53,945
with kidney failure is dangerous.

491
00:31:54,012 --> 00:31:55,346
I know that!

492
00:31:56,281 --> 00:31:57,982
But there is no other way!

493
00:31:58,049 --> 00:31:59,183
I will remove it without cutting.

494
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:01,286
Get out of the way.

495
00:32:03,821 --> 00:32:05,823
No way, Daimon. Say it is inoperable.

496
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:07,659
I decline.

497
00:32:07,725 --> 00:32:10,862
Do you want to kill the patient?
What if you fail?

498
00:32:10,929 --> 00:32:12,430
I never fail.

499
00:32:15,967 --> 00:32:18,236
What is your plan?

500
00:32:18,703 --> 00:32:19,771
I'm going to get it all at once.

501
00:32:20,204 --> 00:32:22,607
I'll separate the lobus caudatus
to have inferior vena cava exposed.

502
00:32:22,674 --> 00:32:23,775
- Lower my magnifier.
- Okay.

503
00:32:24,442 --> 00:32:25,410
- Excuse me.
- How will you

504
00:32:25,476 --> 00:32:27,612
without cutting?

505
00:32:28,046 --> 00:32:29,981
I'm going to pull out the tumour

506
00:32:30,048 --> 00:32:31,683
in the atrium all at once.

507
00:32:32,083 --> 00:32:32,917
Pull out?

508
00:32:32,984 --> 00:32:33,952
You're going to pull it out?

509
00:32:34,018 --> 00:32:35,053
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here.

510
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:36,554
Here you are.

511
00:32:42,827 --> 00:32:45,430
Both assistants, ligate the blood vessel.

512
00:32:45,496 --> 00:32:46,431
Got it.

513
00:32:46,497 --> 00:32:47,565
Suction.

514
00:32:49,167 --> 00:32:50,268
- Monopolar.
- Yes, ma'am.

515
00:32:51,402 --> 00:32:53,371
Raise the blood vessels on the heart.

516
00:33:03,214 --> 00:33:06,584
She is going to pull out
the cancer…that's spread

517
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:08,119
from the liver to the heart.

518
00:33:08,186 --> 00:33:11,222
I see. I didn't even think
about that method.

519
00:33:14,225 --> 00:33:17,095
OPERATING HOUR

520
00:33:17,161 --> 00:33:19,630
Assistant, ligate the vessels
near the hepatic vein.

521
00:33:19,697 --> 00:33:21,299
- Raise it higher.
- Got it.

522
00:33:27,071 --> 00:33:29,674
I have separated them.

523
00:33:29,741 --> 00:33:30,875
Got it.

524
00:33:36,114 --> 00:33:38,549
The THVB is complete. Time it.

525
00:33:38,616 --> 00:33:39,817
Timing.

526
00:33:41,219 --> 00:33:43,788
I will now cut the root of
the right hepatic vein.

527
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:45,023
- Scalpel.
- Here.

528
00:33:48,893 --> 00:33:50,094
- Mosquito clamp.
- Here you are.

529
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:55,533
I'll remove the right lobe and the tumour.

530
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:57,201
REMOVAL OF THE RIGHT LOBE AND
THE TUMOUR

531
00:34:21,826 --> 00:34:23,127
Successfully removed.

532
00:34:25,696 --> 00:34:26,964
Ligate the vein.

533
00:34:27,031 --> 00:34:28,199
Okay.

534
00:34:39,343 --> 00:34:42,947
OPERATING HOUR

535
00:34:49,220 --> 00:34:51,155
- It's complete.
- Blood loss is 700.

536
00:34:51,222 --> 00:34:53,591
Blood pressure of 130 and 75.

537
00:35:04,869 --> 00:35:07,138
- Nice work.
- Good work.

538
00:35:07,205 --> 00:35:09,173
- Good job.
- Thank you.

539
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:12,210
I won.

540
00:35:13,244 --> 00:35:16,814
I won. I won.

541
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:22,153
I won! I won! I won!

542
00:35:23,454 --> 00:35:26,124
Dr. Shrimp. I won!

543
00:35:27,925 --> 00:35:29,327
I won.

544
00:35:29,393 --> 00:35:30,862
The world's first medical case...

545
00:35:32,196 --> 00:35:33,498
is miraculously born here.

546
00:35:40,004 --> 00:35:42,073
What did Ebina win?

547
00:36:01,459 --> 00:36:03,361
It's so bright!

548
00:36:06,130 --> 00:36:08,499
I'm exhausted.

549
00:36:11,235 --> 00:36:13,704
I did it! I followed

550
00:36:13,771 --> 00:36:15,439
the empty theory thesis and realised.

551
00:36:15,506 --> 00:36:18,376
It's the first case.
Let's name it, the Ebina...

552
00:36:18,442 --> 00:36:20,578
- Ebina! Ebina!
- Yes?

553
00:36:20,645 --> 00:36:23,481
How about you sit here?

554
00:36:23,548 --> 00:36:28,119
Why don't you sit on…the chair of the
Director of Toutei University Hospital?

555
00:36:30,154 --> 00:36:31,656
Have you two ever sat here?

556
00:36:32,823 --> 00:36:34,058
Of course not.

557
00:36:34,125 --> 00:36:35,259
You haven't, have you?

558
00:36:35,326 --> 00:36:38,563
You'll be the first one besides me.

559
00:36:38,996 --> 00:36:39,897
Go ahead.

560
00:36:41,098 --> 00:36:44,101
- Well then, excuse me.
- Go ahead.

561
00:36:53,678 --> 00:36:56,948
How does it feel?

562
00:36:57,481 --> 00:37:00,484
Tell these two how great you feel.

563
00:37:01,919 --> 00:37:02,987
It's great!

564
00:37:05,189 --> 00:37:07,592
- Isn't it?
- Yes, sir.

565
00:37:09,026 --> 00:37:10,528
It is great.

566
00:37:10,595 --> 00:37:11,796
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

567
00:37:14,732 --> 00:37:15,866
Oh, Director?

568
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:20,037
Daimon, you really came in
at a perfect time.

569
00:37:20,104 --> 00:37:21,472
You called me over.

570
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,074
Oh, right.

571
00:37:23,841 --> 00:37:27,044
There is something I wanted
to confirm with you.

572
00:37:27,111 --> 00:37:28,479
- What is it?
- Well,

573
00:37:29,747 --> 00:37:34,185
I am informed…that you,
Michiko Daimon, are the one...

574
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:38,856
who performed the surgery
according to the thesis. Is it true?

575
00:37:38,923 --> 00:37:40,157
Of course.

576
00:37:40,224 --> 00:37:42,660
Yes, right.

577
00:37:43,761 --> 00:37:48,766
So that means, Ebina, you didn't operate.

578
00:37:51,469 --> 00:37:52,470
What should I do?

579
00:37:52,536 --> 00:37:56,707
We, at this hospital, cannot lie anymore.

580
00:37:58,075 --> 00:37:59,010
Wait a moment.

581
00:38:00,478 --> 00:38:01,612
Didn't I tell you?

582
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:04,482
No matter what, I will make it a success.

583
00:38:04,849 --> 00:38:07,685
Daimon couldn't do that.

584
00:38:08,119 --> 00:38:09,387
The oath!

585
00:38:10,588 --> 00:38:14,558
Give it to me. The agreement we signed.

586
00:38:15,259 --> 00:38:16,294
Give it to me.

587
00:38:27,471 --> 00:38:29,206
Read this.

588
00:38:29,807 --> 00:38:32,410
"Give a task that Dr. Ebina deserves."

589
00:38:32,843 --> 00:38:37,581
Can I nullify this?

590
00:38:39,116 --> 00:38:41,085
What do you think?

591
00:38:42,119 --> 00:38:43,321
It's okay to just discard this, right?

592
00:38:45,890 --> 00:38:47,925
Answer me.

593
00:38:58,936 --> 00:39:00,504
It's no longer effective.

594
00:39:05,710 --> 00:39:06,677
What will you do with it?

595
00:39:12,583 --> 00:39:15,419
That's it.

596
00:39:17,888 --> 00:39:21,926
You just chewed on all my words...

597
00:39:22,660 --> 00:39:24,128
and didn't listen to what I said.

598
00:39:25,763 --> 00:39:27,064
Can I ask you a favour?

599
00:39:33,404 --> 00:39:35,306
Seriously? Are they goats?

600
00:39:36,707 --> 00:39:38,609
Ebina,

601
00:39:39,577 --> 00:39:42,046
how long are you going to sit there for?

602
00:39:42,747 --> 00:39:43,948
I'm sorry.

603
00:39:48,452 --> 00:39:50,254
There is no longer...

604
00:39:51,155 --> 00:39:54,992
a chair for you...

605
00:39:55,860 --> 00:39:58,028
here in...

606
00:39:58,562 --> 00:40:04,301
Toutei University Hospital.

607
00:40:05,870 --> 00:40:08,606
Thank you for what you've done so far.

608
00:40:12,910 --> 00:40:14,278
Now goodbye.

609
00:40:19,450 --> 00:40:21,051
Goodbye.

610
00:40:25,589 --> 00:40:27,425
- Excuse me.
- Come in!

611
00:40:27,491 --> 00:40:29,560
Dr. Ebina.

612
00:40:29,627 --> 00:40:31,028
Goodbye.

613
00:40:31,495 --> 00:40:33,297
I see you paid the price.

614
00:40:35,166 --> 00:40:36,200
Excuse me.

615
00:40:43,874 --> 00:40:46,243
Michiko, please wait outside.

616
00:40:46,577 --> 00:40:49,780
Okay. Excuse me.

617
00:40:52,583 --> 00:40:53,684
Director Hiruma,

618
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:57,021
congratulations on your success.

619
00:40:58,122 --> 00:40:59,256
Here is your bill.

620
00:40:59,957 --> 00:41:01,392
Bill?

621
00:41:02,359 --> 00:41:04,829
I don't recall asking for your
people to operate.

622
00:41:05,763 --> 00:41:08,666
What do you plan to do about this thesis?

623
00:41:10,768 --> 00:41:13,537
You cannot publish it
with Michiko Daimon's name.

624
00:41:14,371 --> 00:41:19,076
However, you can't easily give up on this.

625
00:41:21,078 --> 00:41:22,680
This is the first case in the world.

626
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:25,950
That is true.

627
00:41:27,751 --> 00:41:30,588
I would like to find someone...

628
00:41:30,654 --> 00:41:33,123
who would like their name on the thesis.

629
00:41:38,529 --> 00:41:39,830
Please sign on this note.

630
00:41:39,897 --> 00:41:41,098
A note?

631
00:41:42,199 --> 00:41:43,300
Here is a pen.

632
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:46,604
Here is your melon.

633
00:42:00,017 --> 00:42:01,385
I have a pen.

634
00:42:04,555 --> 00:42:06,090
I have a melon.

635
00:42:10,794 --> 00:42:13,030
Pen melon pen melon pen melon pen!

636
00:42:16,100 --> 00:42:19,436
I managed to survive.

637
00:42:24,909 --> 00:42:27,678
I'm really glad you operated on me.

638
00:42:29,647 --> 00:42:31,448
Thank you so much.

639
00:42:33,117 --> 00:42:35,352
I am not the one who operated.

640
00:42:35,419 --> 00:42:37,121
- What?
- It was Daimon.

641
00:42:41,492 --> 00:42:44,595
She's much more skilled
at performing surgery.

642
00:42:44,662 --> 00:42:46,230
Oh my.

643
00:42:49,133 --> 00:42:52,269
I am the one who should thank you.

644
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:56,440
Thanks to you,

645
00:42:57,741 --> 00:42:59,343
I could have a bigger dream.

646
00:43:00,978 --> 00:43:01,912
A bigger dream?

647
00:43:02,313 --> 00:43:03,581
Even though it ended in an instant.

648
00:43:04,648 --> 00:43:07,651
Did you take down Hiruma?

649
00:43:13,257 --> 00:43:14,391
It was exciting.

650
00:43:16,460 --> 00:43:17,828
The first time I felt that way
since becoming a doctor.

651
00:43:18,829 --> 00:43:20,898
That's amazing.

652
00:43:33,811 --> 00:43:37,414
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

653
00:43:37,915 --> 00:43:39,850
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

654
00:43:40,451 --> 00:43:44,855
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

655
00:43:45,489 --> 00:43:48,425
<i>Her solo weapons are</i>
<i>her license and the skills</i>

656
00:43:48,993 --> 00:43:50,260
<i>she has earned.</i>

657
00:43:51,362 --> 00:43:52,196
Daimon!

658
00:43:57,401 --> 00:44:01,605
Do you think…I lost a battle
that I must have won?

659
00:44:03,007 --> 00:44:05,242
You look scary.

660
00:44:05,309 --> 00:44:07,011
Victory or defeat as a doctor
doesn't matter to me.

661
00:44:07,811 --> 00:44:09,380
What matters is the patient.

662
00:44:12,282 --> 00:44:13,751
This is what you said in the past.

663
00:44:15,052 --> 00:44:17,588
No way, I didn't say that
in the past. I'm still young.

664
00:44:19,423 --> 00:44:20,624
I'm leaving tonight.

665
00:44:20,691 --> 00:44:21,925
Whatever.

666
00:44:21,992 --> 00:44:24,762
You can work in Kanazawa whenever you
want to. I'll treat you to a nice meal.

667
00:44:25,796 --> 00:44:29,066
- Really?
- Of course.

668
00:44:33,303 --> 00:44:35,606
What is it? You look scary.

669
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:37,808
She has it, too.

670
00:44:38,242 --> 00:44:41,078
I don't think we speak the same language.
Bye.

671
00:44:41,979 --> 00:44:44,381
I feel terrible.

672
00:44:52,089 --> 00:44:53,924
Michiko!

673
00:44:54,525 --> 00:44:56,727
Akira.

674
00:44:56,794 --> 00:44:59,029
I'll buy you the dress.

675
00:44:59,096 --> 00:45:00,230
I don't need it.

676
00:45:00,297 --> 00:45:01,231
Why not?

677
00:45:01,298 --> 00:45:04,034
Buy me some meat. Yakiniku is fine...

678
00:45:04,101 --> 00:45:05,536
Anything will do!

679
00:45:05,602 --> 00:45:07,705
I want to binge eat!

680
00:45:07,771 --> 00:45:10,107
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

681
00:45:10,674 --> 00:45:13,444
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

682
00:45:14,378 --> 00:45:16,847
I hear sounds in my head.

683
00:45:16,914 --> 00:45:18,949
Please fix Nanao's ears.

684
00:45:19,016 --> 00:45:21,785
The world class surgeon...
Kitano, will perform it.

685
00:45:21,852 --> 00:45:23,187
I will not have surgery.

686
00:45:23,654 --> 00:45:25,122
You're too arrogant!
